### 10. Remove the old purchase mirrors when Phase 3 lands

The current successful purchase path still performs:

* `mirrorPurchasedTicket()`;
* `refreshPurchasedEvent()`;
* ticket-hook invalidation;
* global overlay success;
* timed redirect to My Tickets.

Once Phase 3 is implemented, these must not continue alongside the new operation service. Leaving them in place would produce exactly the duplicated architecture the plan is trying to avoid.

Phase 3 should remove purchase-specific use of:

* `readModelSync`;
* `invalidateTickets`;
* `onPurchaseComplete`;
* timed success dismissal;
* automatic navigation to `/tickets`.

After confirmation, navigate explicitly to:

```text
/purchases/:operationId
```

Phase 4 alone should introduce trusted ticket and supply reconciliation. Until then:

* the receipt succeeds at `chain_confirmed`;
* My Tickets may not yet contain the ticket;
* “View ticket” remains hidden;
* the user is never asked to pay again to repair the missing mirror.

This preserves the intended Phase 3/Phase 4 boundary instead of implementing half of Phase 4 twice.   

